# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you need.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED. The app is fully functional with an empty file:
# resume data lives in your browser, and the JSON Resume import/export,
# file import/export and all local features work without any configuration.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive backup (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables "Back up to Google Drive" in the editor header.
#
# A client ID is PUBLIC by design — it identifies the app to Google, it does not
# authorise anything on its own. That is why it can live in a VITE_ variable.
# Never put a client SECRET here: VITE_ variables are inlined into the shipped
# JavaScript, so a secret would be published to every visitor.
#
# How to create one:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   2. Create Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application
#   3. Authorised JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173 and your deploy URL
#   4. Enable the "Google Drive API" for the project
#   5. Paste the client ID below
#
# Scope requested: drive.file — the app can only see files IT created. It cannot
# read the rest of your Drive. Do not widen this without a very good reason.
#
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI features (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave this EMPTY for any public deploy. VITE_ variables are inlined into the
# shipped bundle, so a key set here becomes plain text in dist/assets/*.js and
# will be scraped. The build now REFUSES to run if this is set (see
# forbidInlineAiKey in vite.config.js).
#
# Users enter their own key in AI Settings instead; it is stored in their own
# browser and never sent anywhere except the provider they chose.
#
# VITE_AI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Job agent (optional, local only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The apply agent runs on your own machine. It binds to 127.0.0.1 and has no
# authentication, so it must never be exposed to a network.
#
# JOB_DISCOVERY_PORT=3457
# HOST=127.0.0.1
